{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.about.liquid
  ────────────────────────────────────
  Alternate page template. In the admin: Pages → About → Template suffix →
  "about". Renders inside layout/theme.liquid, which supplies <main>.

  Requires:
      {{ 'hivolt.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
      {{ 'hivolt-pages.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  The copy here is the honest version, and it is deliberately the honest
  version. HIVOLT selects manufacturer blanks; it does not own a factory. That
  is stated in the first paragraph rather than buried, because the entire
  argument of the site — we publish the specification while the category
  publishes adjectives — only works if the unflattering part is published too.

  Nothing on this page is invented: no founding date, no founder, no team, no
  factory visit, no mill tour. Every fact below is one the store can stand
  behind. If a fact is not here, it is because we do not have it.

  Any body copy entered on the page in the admin renders after the sections, so
  the template can be extended without editing this file.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign contact_url = pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact' -%}
{%- assign support_email = shop.email | default: 'support@hivolt-usa.com' -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'About' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">About HIVOLT</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">We don't own<br>the factory.<br><em>We publish the spec.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    HIVOLT sells manufacturer blanks. We choose them, specify them and list them
    under our own name — we do not make them in a factory we own, and we are not
    going to imply otherwise. What we do that the category does not is tell you
    exactly what the garment is: fibre composition, and fabric weight in grams
    per square metre.
  </p>
  <div class="hero__cta">
    <a class="btn" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Shop the range</a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pages/fabric">How we measure</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── the position ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <h2 class="sec__h">The position</h2>
    <span class="mono">Why this store exists</span>
  </div>

  <div class="pg__cols">
    <div class="rte">
      <p>
        Most activewear under a hundred dollars is the same trade. A brand picks
        garments from a manufacturer's existing range, puts a name on them and
        sells them. That is what we do. The part almost nobody does is publish the
        specification of what they picked.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the category and you will be told a legging is soft, sculpting,
        weightless, made for movement. You will rarely be told what it is made of
        by percentage, and almost never what the fabric weighs. Fabric weight —
        grams per square metre — is knit density, and knit density is what decides
        whether a legging stays opaque when it is stretched across a squat. It is
        the one number that answers the question everybody actually has, and it is
        the number the category leaves off.
      </p>
      <p>
        So that is the whole position. Every style we list carries its fibre
        composition and its fabric weight in g/m², copied from the supplier's
        specification sheet without editing. If a figure is unflattering it stays
        on the page. If we do not have a figure, the row is left out rather than
        filled with a guess.
      </p>
      <p>
        Being a selector rather than a manufacturer is not a weakness we are
        hiding — it is the reason the specification matters. We cannot tell you
        about looms we do not operate. We can tell you precisely what we selected
        and what it measures, and you can hold that number against anything else
        you are considering. Nobody in this price range makes that comparison
        easy, which is exactly why it is worth publishing.
      </p>
      <p>
        HIVOLT is new. There are no customer reviews on this site because no
        customer has written one yet. We ship within the United States only, out
        of a facility in Illinois, and orders take 8&ndash;14 business days. All
        three of those sentences would read better if they were untrue. They are
        not, so they stay.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">
      <p class="mono pg__aside-h">HIVOLT, stated plainly</p>
      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Model</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Manufacturer blanks</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Published per style</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>Composition + g/m²</em></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Customer reviews</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">None yet</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Dispatched from</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Illinois, USA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Delivery</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">8&ndash;14 business days</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Shipping</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Free, no minimum</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Ships to</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">United States only</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Returns</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">60 days, unworn</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Checkout</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Shopify Checkout</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Support</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">{{ support_email }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sheet__src">
        Specification values come from the supplier's sheet. Shipping and returns
        figures are the store's own published terms.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── what we won't do ────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <h2 class="sec__h">What we won't do</h2>
    <span class="mono">The absences are deliberate</span>
  </div>
  <div class="trust__grid">
    <div class="trust__c">
      <div class="trust__k">Not here</div>
      <p class="trust__v">Reviews we don't have</p>
      <p class="trust__d">
        HIVOLT is new and nobody has written one. There is no widget on this site
        pretending otherwise. When real ones exist we will publish them, including
        the ones that are not kind.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__c">
      <div class="trust__k">Not here</div>
      <p class="trust__v">Urgency</p>
      <p class="trust__d">
        No timers, no stock counters, no offer that resets when you reload the
        page. The price on the product is the price at checkout.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__c">
      <div class="trust__k">Not here</div>
      <p class="trust__v">Health claims</p>
      <p class="trust__d">
        A legging is clothing. Nothing on this site will tell you it treats a
        condition, and we will not sell one as though it does.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__c">
      <div class="trust__k">Not here</div>
      <p class="trust__v">A founder myth</p>
      <p class="trust__d">
        No garage, no origin story, no dated milestones we cannot evidence. The
        specification is the argument. It either holds up against what you compare
        it to or it does not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if page.content != blank -%}
  <section class="pg wrap">
    <div class="rte">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

<!-- ── questions ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">Questions?</span>
      Anything this page does not answer, ask and we will answer it in writing.
      Replies within one business day.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ contact_url }}">Contact us</a>
  </div>
</section>
